      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ اَلرَّجُلِ هَلْ يَرِثُ دَارَ اِمْرَأَتِهِ وَ أَرْضَهَا مِنَ اَلتُّرْبَةِ شَيْئاً أَوْ يَكُونُ فِي ذَلِكَ بِمَنْزِلَةِ اَلْمَرْأَةِ فَلاَ يَرِثُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ شَيْئاً فَقَالَ \"يَرِثُهَا وَ تَرِثُهُ مِنْ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ تَرَكَ وَ تَرَكَتْ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5753 - Aban narrated from Al-Faḍl ibn Abd Al-Malik or Ibn Abi Yaʿfur from Abu Abdullah (as) who said:\n\"I asked Imam (as) about a man - does he inherit his wife's house and land from the soil, or is he like the woman who does not inherit anything from that?\"\nImam (as) replied: \"He inherits from her, and she inherits from him, from everything either of them leaves behind.\""
        ]
      }
    },
